"Internal Error ()\nciteturn216view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.kkk.tsk.tr/kkksablonmaster/header/hizmetler/okullar/KKAMYO/index.html\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://www.kkk.tsk.tr/kkksablonmaster/header/hizmetler/okullar/KKAMYO/index.html: (502) Bad Gateway--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn216view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://elektrik.btu.edu.tr/tr/sayfa/iletisim\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://elektrik.btu.edu.tr/tr/sayfa/iletisim is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.iitp.ac.in/acad/files/phdadmissionbrochure.pdf)\nciteturn216view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 25; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.iitp.ac.in/acad/files/phdadmissionbrochure.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 753\nL0@P0: Information Brochure\nL1@P0: for\nL2@P0: PhD Admissions\nL3@P0: INDIAN INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY PATNA\nL4@P0: BIHTA, PATNA, BIHAR 801106\nL5@P0-1: Page 1 of 25A General\nL6@P1: 1. Message to Candidate\nL7@P1: 2. The Institute\nL8@P1: 3. Important Date/Academic Calendar\nL9@P1: 4. Research Facilities\nL10@P1: 5. Student Amenities + Hostel Accommodation\nL11@P1: 6. Ph.D. Programme\nL12@P1: 7. Eligibility Criterion for Admission + General Guidelines\nL13@P1: 8. Application Categories and Financial Support\nL14@P1: 9. Admission Procedure\nL15@P1: 10. Payment of Fees and Deposits + Fee Structure + Mess Fee\nL16@P1: 11. Registration for the Ph.D. Degree\nL17@P1: 12. Confirmation f Registration\nL18@P1: 13. Submission of Thesis and Award of Degree + Credit System\nL19@P1: 14. Reservation of Seats\nL20@P1: B Department and Disciplines\nL21@P1: 1. Computer Science & Engineering\nL22@P1: 2. Electrical Engineering\nL23@P1: 3. Mechanical Engineering\nL24@P1: 4. Material Science & Engineering\nL25@P1: 5. Chemical & Biochemical Engineering\nL26@P1: 6. Civil & Environmental Engineering\nL27@P1: 7. Physics\nL28@P1: 8. Chemistry\nL29@P1: 9. Math\nL30@P1: 10. Humanities & Social Sciences\nL31@P1: C Centre of Excellence\nL32@P1: 1. SAIF\nL33@P1: D Appendices\nL34@P1: 1. Fees and Deposits + Refund of FEE\nL35@P1: 2. Refund of Fee\nL36@P1: 3. Financial Assistance\nL37@P1-2: Page 2 of 254. Sponsorship letter for full-time candidates\nL38@P2: 5. Employer’s Letter in case of candidates joining Ph.D. programme on Study leave\nL39@P2: 6. Sponsorship Certificate for External Registration\nL40@P2: 7. No Objection Certificate for college Teacher\nL41@P2: 8. Co-Guide particulars of External Registration\nL42@P2: E How to reach Institute\nL43@P2: F International Student Admission\nL44@P2: G Important contact number\nL45@P2: A-GENERAL\nL46@P2: Message to Candidate\nL47@P2: Indian Institute of Technology Patna is an Institution of National Importance and a new addition to the\nL48@P2: hallowed IIT System that has proven its worth in last 50+ years. The alumni of IIT are internationally\nL49@P2: known for their caliber and contribution. Since its inception in 2008, IIT Patna- like its young as well as\nL50@P2: established peers- has pursued excellence with steadfast determination.\nL51@P2: IITP has 6 Engineering Disciplines: Civil and Environmental Engineering, Chemical and Biochemical\nL52@P2: Engineering, Computer Science and Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering and\nL53@P2: Material Science and Engineering; 2 Science Disciplines: Physics and Chemistry; Humanities and Social\nL54@P2: Sciences; Mathematics. Its faculty members are experts in their respective fields. The thriving PhD,\nL55@P2: M.Tech and B.Tech programs of IITP see the students and faculty publish prolifically, win competitions,\nL56@P2: come up with innovations and build societal awareness.\nL57@P2: For impact, technology has to understand its vital links with (i) Humanities and Social Sciences, (ii)\nL58@P2: Mathematics and (iii) Natural Sciences. Technology can change life if it can acquire “Perspective” from\nL59@P2: Humanities and Social Sciences, “Technique” from Mathematics and “Foundations” from Sciences. In\nL60@P2: IITP, we will strive to achieve this 4-way harmony of Technology, Humanities and Social Sciences,\nL61@P2: Basic Sciences and Mathematics. The original charter of new IITs, viz., interdisciplinary research and\nL62@P2: teaching will thereby be addressed.\nL63@P2: IITP is strategically placed, geographically speaking. The stretch from Gujarat to Manipur has 11 IITs\nL64@P2: (Gandhinagr, Jodhpur, Mandi, Ropar, Roorkee, Delhi, Kanpur, Patna, Kharagpur, Bhubaneshwar and\nL65@P2: Guahati) and a large number of NITs and renowned universities. This sets up a tremendous powerhouse\nL66@P2: of knowledge and high quality human resource. Additionally, the state of Bihar is rich with tradition and\nL67@P2: resources, emphasizes education, is blessed with the fertile Gangetic plain and abundant sunlight. This\nL68@P2: paves way for immense societal impact through agriculture and energy technology, amongst many other\nL69@P2: possibilities.\nL70@P2-3: Page 3 of 25IITP has moved to its brand new campus at Bihta, a place with history, about 35 KM from main city\nL71@P3: Patna. The sprawling 501 acre campus houses four academic complexes for the departments, a Class\nL72@P3: Rooms Complex, Student, Faculty and Staff Residential quarters, Hospital and School and an impressive\nL73@P3: Administrative building. The 2015 autumn session in IITP started from the new campus in Bihta.\nL74@P3: At this juncture of history, IIT Patna is poised for great things.\nL75@P3: Director, IIT Patna\nL76@P3: The Institute\nL77@P3: Indian Institute of Technology Patna is one of the new IITs established by an Act of the Indian Parliament\nL78@P3: on August 06, 2008. Patna which was known as Patliputra has been a center of knowledge since long has\nL79@P3: been attracting visitors and scholars from many parts of the world such as China, Indonesia, Japan, Korea,\nL80@P3: Sri Lanka, among others. This has been a land of visionaries. Some of the legends from this region\nL81@P3: include Lord Gautam Buddha, Lord Mahavir, Guru Gobind Singh, the famous astronomer Aryabhatta and\nL82@P3: the first President of India, Dr. Rajendra Prasad.\nL83@P3: IIT Patna has ten departments: These are Computer Science & Engineering, Electrical Engineering,\nL84@P3: Mechanical Engineering, Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Civil & Environmental Engineering,\nL85@P3: Materials Science & Engineering, Chemistry, Physics, Mathematics and Humanities & Social Science\nL86@P3: departments.\nL87@P3: IIT Patna campus is located at Bihta which is approximately 40 kms from Patna. For driving directions\nL88@P3: and contact details, please point your browser to the following link:\nL89@P3: http://www.iitp.ac.in/index.php/contact.html\nL90@P3: The Institute has developed modern facilities that are fully equipped with the state-of-the-art facilities\nL91@P3: (equipment software and machines) that are routinely used to train and educate students in the following\nL92@P3: programs:\nL93@P3: B.Tech in five disciplines: Computer Science and Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical\nL94@P3: Engineering, Civil Engineering and Chemical Engineering. M.Tech in multi-disciplinary streams with\nL95@P3: eight specializations:\nL96@P3: Mechatronics jointly offered by Departments of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, Mathematics &\nL97@P3: Computing jointly offered by Departments of Mathematics and Computer Science & Engineering, Nano\nL98@P3: Science & Technology jointly offered by Departments of Physics and Chemistry, Computer Science and\nL99@P3: Engineering offered by Department of Computer Science & Engineering, Communication System\nL100@P3: Engineering offered by Department of Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering offered by\nL101@P3: Department of Mechanical Engineering, Civil and Infrastructure Engineering offered by Department of\nL102@P3: Civil & Environmental Engineering and Materials Science and Engineering offered by Department of\nL103@P3: Materials Science and Engineering.\nL104@P3: Budding research scholars are admitted in the PhD program of this Institute in all ten (10) departments.\nL105@P3-4: Page 4 of 25As of April 2016, IIT Patna has six hundred seventy students enrolled in its B Tech programs, one\nL106@P4: hundred sixty one M.Tech students and two hundred fifty nine Ph.D students. Since inception in 2008 and\nL107@P4: till April 2016, more than four hundred students have been awarded B.Tech. degree, more than seventy\nL108@P4: five students have been awarded M.Tech. degree and more than 20 research scholars have been awarded\nL109@P4: PhD degree.As of April 2016, faculty strength of IIT Patna is one hundred one (which includes one DST\nL110@P4: Ramanujan Faculty Fellow, one Adjunct Faculty, one DST INSPIRE Faculty and one Visiting Professor).\nL111@P4: Faculty members are supported by more that seventy efficient staff (non-teaching) members. These\nL112@P4: numbers are anticipated to increase as the Institute is growing at a steady pace. The faculty members of\nL113@P4: IIT Patna have a wide range of academic and research experience. They have been trained in the top\nL114@P4: ranked Institutes within the country and abroad.\nL115@P4: Research activity in IIT Patna has been published in high quality and peer-reviewed national and\nL116@P4: international journals. Faculty members of IIT Patna have been also participating in national and\nL117@P4: international conferences of repute.\nL118@P4: Academic Calendar – please follow the given link\nL119@P4:  http://www.iitp.ac.in/acad/academic_calendar.php\nL120@P4-5: Page 5 of 254. Research Facilities\nL121@P5: The institute has state of the art research facilities. Incubation centres are functioning very well.\nL122@P5: 5. Student Amenities + Hostel Accommodation\nL123@P5: Students' Gymkhana\nL124@P5: The students' gymkhana of IIT Patna(established in\nL125@P5: 2008) is the Students' Governing Council\nL126@P5: consisting of the elected student representatives\nL127@P5: working for the over-all well being and holistic\nL128@P5: development of students in the institute.\nL129@P5: The elected representatives of the students\nL130@P5: from each hostel strive to foster growth and\nL131@P5: leadership among the students by coordinating\nL132@P5: various events helping to extract the maximum\nL133@P5: of ones talent. To promote the co-curricular\nL134@P5: activities and interests, the gymkhana has\nL135@P5: many clubs and groups dedicated to the\nL136@P5: interests of the students.\nL137@P5: Sports at IIT Patna bring together relaxation and competition getting the best of every player. It\nL138@P5: organizes various inter-hostel and inter-department competitions.\nL139@P5: The blending of different cultures has lent uniqueness to the cultural activities which are\nL140@P5: organized throughout the year. The organization of various workshops, seminars and various\nL141@P5: technical activities at IIT P makes learning an enjoyable experience.\nL142@P5: IIT Patna currently has one boys' hostel and one temporary girls' hostel in the campus. It also has\nL143@P5: necessary arrangements for married research scholars. More boys and girls hostels are in the\nL144@P5: process of construction. The boys' hostel is at a distance of about 1KM from the academic\nL145@P5: complex and the girls' hostel is situated near the faculty quarters, about 3 KMs from academic\nL146@P5: complex. Presently over 1200 students are residing in the hostels. Regular bus services have been\nL147@P5: provided from the hostels to and the academic buildings. Students have access to Wi-Fi\nL148@P5: connectivity throughout the buildings. In addition to the adequate health care facilities, all the\nL149@P5: students are covered under Vidyarthi Mediclaim Insurance Policy. The hostel is equipped with\nL150@P5: gymnasium, TV room and table tennis facilities. Campus has a basketball court, a volleyball\nL151@P5: court, and badminton court. A football-cum-cricket ground will also be available very soon.\nL152@P5: There are two students' mess in boys' hostel and one mess in the girls' hostel, along with various\nL153@P5-6: Page 6 of 25food joints and canteen in the Food court. The students elect a student body once every year in\nL154@P6: the month of April.\nL155@P6: Building\nL156@P6: The boys' hostel building is a 8-storey\nL157@P6: structure divided into 4 blocks viz. A,B,C,D.\nL158@P6: It's spread onto an area of 28849 Sqm. It has\nL159@P6: 912 rooms, all with a balcony, window,\nL160@P6: cupboard, and enough niches. The hostel has\nL161@P6: two common rooms used for recreational\nL162@P6: and co-curricular activities and a\nL163@P6: gymnasium. There are total of 6 lifts in the\nL164@P6: building. Watercoolers are installed on each\nL165@P6: floor. Fire extinguishers and other safety\nL166@P6: measures are taken care of. The building can\nL167@P6: resist high magnitude earthquakes. There are\nL168@P6: seven more such boys hostels and 2 girls\nL169@P6: hostels are proposed in the plan.\nL170@P6: Gymnasium\nL171@P6: Boys hostel has a gymnasium on the first floor\nL172@P6: along side the common room. It has all the\nL173@P6: basic exercise equipments like dumbbells,\nL174@P6: barbells, bench press, etc. It also has other\nL175@P6: major equipments like tredmills, exercise bike,\nL176@P6: squat station, hammer strength machine,\nL177@P6: cables and pulleys, lat pull down machine, leg\nL178@P6: extension machine and few more.\nL179@P6-7: Page 7 of 25Mess\nL180@P7: Boys' Hostel has two mess halls on the ground\nL181@P7: floor and girls' hostel has one. They provide\nL182@P7: breakfast, lunch, snacks and dinner. Messes\nL183@P7: follow a specific menu for the week. Every\nL184@P7: month, the mess menu gets changed.\nL185@P7: Coffee/tea is provided in the breakfast and\nL186@P7: snacks time. Students elects a mess secretary\nL187@P7: from all the years to look after mess related\nL188@P7: issues. Messes are kept clean and work in\nL189@P7: hygienic conditions.\nL190@P7: 6. Ph.D. Programme\nL191@P7: The Ph.D. program in IIT Patna has started in Engineering, Science and Humanities & Social\nL192@P7: Sciences departments since July 2009. Faculty members at IIT Patna have diverse areas of\nL193@P7: research. Students enrolled in PhD program in IIT Patna are guided to do high quality research.\nL194@P7: Relevant departments are equipped with state-of-art research equipment and have access to peer\nL195@P7: reviewed journals. Ph.D. Supervisors in IIT Patna are committed to mentor research scholars and\nL196@P7: groom them for successful careers.\nL197@P7: IIT Patna also promotes and encourages interdisciplinary research, in which case two or more\nL198@P7: departments and centers contribute to innovative and cross-boundary research. Faculty members\nL199@P7: from various departments, centers and schools across the campus are exploring research areas\nL200@P7: that must involve extensive interaction of different traditional disciplines.\nL201@P7: IIT Patna publishes PhD program advertisement twice a year (in the months of March-April and\nL202@P7: September-October) in internet as well as newspaper. Admission in PhD program of IIT Patna to\nL203@P7: all categories of students is granted on the basis of interview/admission test held tentatively in\nL204@P7: the month of December and May - July every year.\nL205@P7-8: Page 8 of 257. Eligibility Criteria for Admission & General Guidelines\nL206@P8: In all the disciplines, the upper age limit is 28 years (B.Tech./B.E./M.Sc./MA/MCA/MBA) and 32\nL207@P8: years (M.Tech./M.E./M.S./M.Phil.) to be calculated from the last date for receiving the application\nL208@P8: form and is applicable only for candidates applying in Regular and Full time category (Institute\nL209@P8: Fellows). Upper age is relaxed up to 05 years in case of candidate belonging to Schedule\nL210@P8: Castes/Schedule Tribes, Women, Physically Handicapped and OBC applicants For admission to the\nL211@P8: PhD Programme in Engineering Department, a candidate must satisfy one of the following criteria:\nL212@P8: A.1.1 Candidates having M.Tech./M.E. degree in a Engineering/Technology, with a minimum CPI of\nL213@P8: 6.5 or 60% of marks.\nL214@P8: A.1.2 Bachelor’s degree in Engineering/Technology in a relevant area with a minimum CPI of 6.5 or\nL215@P8: 60% of marks.\nL216@P8: A.1.3. Master’s degree in Science in a relevant area with a minimum CPI of 6.5 or 60% of marks.\nL217@P8: A.2 PhD in Science\nL218@P8: For admission to the PhD Programme in Science departments, a candidate must satisfy one of the\nL219@P8: following criteria:\nL220@P8: A.2.1 M. Phil. or Master’s degree in Science in a relevant area with a minimum CPI of 6.5 or 60% of\nL221@P8: marks.\nL222@P8: A.2.2 Master’s degree in Engineering/Technology in a relevant area with a minimum CPI of 6.5 or\nL223@P8: 60% of marks.\nL224@P8: A.2.3 Bachelor’s degree in Engineering/Technology in a relevant area with a minimum CPI of 6.5 or\nL225@P8: 60% of marks.\nL226@P8: A.3 PhD in Humanities and Social Sciences\nL227@P8: For admission to the PhD Programme in the department of Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS),\nL228@P8: a candidate must satisfy one of the following criteria:\nL229@P8: A.3.1 M. Phil. or Master’s degree in Arts/Commerce/Science/Management in a relevant area with\nL230@P8: a minimum of 55% marks or equivalent.\nL231@P8: A.3.2 Master’s degree in Engineering/Technology/Design in a relevant area with a minimum CPI of\nL232@P8: 6.5 or 60% marks.\nL233@P8: A.3.3 Bachelor’s degree in Engineering/Technology in a relevant area with a minimum CPI of 6.5 or\nL234@P8: 60% of marks.\nL235@P8: Direct Admission (Waiver of Written Test):\nL236@P8: Sciences, Engineering &Technology:\nL237@P8: The Institute may admit exceptionally bright students and Full-time (Institute Fellows) directly\nL238@P8: (i.e., without written test) into the Ph.D. program.\nL239@P8: Eligible candidates meeting one of the following criteria may\nL240@P8: be considered for a waiver of the written test:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nמפה - יצירת קשר ודרכי הגעה | אוניברסיטת ת\"א | אוניברסיטת תל אביב (https://www.tau.ac.il/gc-map-test)\nciteturn216view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.tau.ac.il/gc-map-test\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 168\nL0: 【0†Image†www.facebook.com】 【1†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2:   * 【2†תפריט עליון】\nL3:   * 【3†תפריט ראשי】\nL4:   * 【4†תוכן ראשי】\nL5: \nL6: 【5†מערכת פניות†tau-int.formtitan.com】【6†אזור אישי לסטודנטים.יות†my.tau.ac.il】【7†להרשמה†www.ims.tau.ac.il】\nL7:   * 【8†אודות】\nL8:     * האוניברסיטה שלנו\nL9:       * 【9†אסטרטגיה】\nL10:       * 【10†חדשות】\nL11:       * 【11†אירועים】\nL12:       * 【12†מגילת כבוד ופרסים】\nL13:       * 【13†זוכרים את הנופלים】\nL14:       * 【14†נשיאי אוניברסיטת תל אביב】\nL15:       * 【15†שוויון, מגוון וקהילה†diversity.tau.ac.il】\nL16:       * 【16†קשרי תעשייה וחברה】\nL17:       * 【17†קמפוס ירוק†greencampus.tau.ac.il】\nL18:     * סגל ומנהלה\nL19:       * 【18†אגפים ומשרדי מנהלה】\nL20:       * 【19†דבר הנשיא】\nL21:       * 【20†דבר הרקטורית†rector.tau.ac.il】\nL22:       * 【21†סנאט האוניברסיטה†acad-sec.tau.ac.il】\nL23:       * 【22†חברי הוועד המנהל】\nL24:       * 【23†המזכירות האקדמית†acad-sec.tau.ac.il】\nL25:       * 【24†אגף רישום ומינהל תלמידים】\nL26:       * 【25†דרושים - משרות אקדמיות】\nL27:       * 【26†דרושים - משרות מינהליות】\nL28:     * מידע שימושי\nL29:       * 【27†יצירת קשר ודרכי הגעה】\nL30:       * 【28†מפת הקמפוס†www2.tau.ac.il】\nL31:       * 【29†מכרזים†tenders.tau.ac.il】\nL32:       * 【30†שירותי מחשוב】\nL33:       * 【31†מידע לשעת חירום】\nL34:       * 【32†לוח שנת הלימודים】\nL35:     *   * 【33†יח